[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644374823","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113827#issuecomment-3644374823","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113827","id":3644374823,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZOL8n","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-12T00:27:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-12T00:27:07Z","body":"I think I get the zest of whats going on here but haven't seen this happen on any other runtimes.\n\nMy guess is that if we get invalid view pose data, we might still be rendering and submitting a frame and as we provide the pose data, there is likely a more serious issue happening in the compositors reprojection.\n\nBy reusing the previous frame pose data we circumvent this, but the real solution may be to ensure that we don't render this frame.\n\nNeed to look into this further.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3644374823/reactions",